backed by two loopback-file physical volumes since no spare block device existed, formatted ext4 and mounted it at /srv/data. Wrote test data, then grew the LV online (while mounted) from ~1000MiB to ~2.15GiB via vgextend + lvextend + resize2fs, verifying data integrity throughout. Set up persistence across reboot via a systemd oneshot unit (lvm-loopback.service) that reattaches the loop devices and activates the VG before local-fs-pre.target, referenced from /etc/fstab via x-systemd.requires. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id and healthy mount/data state, issued systemctl reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified /srv/data remounted automatically at 2.1G with both test files passing sha256sum verification.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 disk layout: single 20G vda fully allocated to root/boot, no spare block device or partition available for a native PV\",\"Created two 1200M backing files under /var/lib/lvmfiles and attached them as /dev/loop20 and /dev/loop21\",\"pvcreate on loop20, vgcreate vgdata, lvcreate lvdata (1000M), mkfs.ext4, mounted at /srv/data\",\"Wrote testfile.txt and bigfile.txt to /srv/data and recorded sha256 checksums\",\"pvcreate on loop21, vgextend vgdata with loop21, lvextend +1200M, resize2fs run online while filesystem stayed mounted; final size <2.15GiB / 2.1G reported by df\",\"Verified checksums matched post-extend and confirmed LV remained mounted read-write\",\"Created /etc/systemd/system/lvm-loopback.service (oneshot; reattaches both loop devices, runs udevadm settle, vgchange -ay vgdata before local-fs-pre.target) and enabled it\",\"Added /etc/fstab entry for /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata -> /srv/data with x-systemd.requires=lvm-loopback.service,nofail\",\"Simulated boot-time reassembly by unmounting, deactivating the VG, and detaching the loop devices, then starting the service + mount -a; fixed an incorrect /sbin/udevadm path in the unit during this test; confirmed clean automatic reassembly with intact data\",\"Captured pre-reboot boot_id (92ec88af...) and confirmed healthy mount, size, and checksums\",\"Issued sudo systemctl reboot on node1; connection dropped confirming the command was accepted before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed new boot_id (2d40a3de...), proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Verified post-reboot: /srv/data auto-mounted via the new systemd unit + fstab, size 2.1G (>=2GB), lvm-loopback.service active, and both test files passed sha256sum verification\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"LV mounted at /srv/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0a31dd120e81439e\"],\"summary\":\"df -h shows /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata mounted at /srv/data after lvcreate/mkfs/mount\"},{\"requirement\":\"LV grown to >=2GB while staying mounted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fad00e5e25e04d20\"],\"summary\":\"vgextend + lvextend + online resize2fs performed while /srv/data was mounted; lvextend reports growth to <2.15 GiB and df shows 2.1G on /srv/data still mounted\"},{\"requirement\":\"Contents stay intact through the extend\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0a31dd120e81439e\",\"cmd-ce9533c26ebe479f\"],\"summary\":\"sha256 checksums of testfile.txt and bigfile.txt recorded before extend and verified OK immediately after the online resize\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persistence mechanism configured for reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-96f8c8e34768425c\",\"cmd-d90c3127e805474d\",\"cmd-c00e1dedd79b424c\"],\"summary\":\"systemd lvm-loopback.service enabled, fstab entry added referencing it, and a simulated teardown/reassembly (detach loops, deactivate VG, restart service, mount -a) proved the automatic reassembly logic works with data intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a2babb3152494952\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 92ec88af..., confirmed /srv/data mounted at 2.1G, and sha256sum -c passed for both test files before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement / command accepted before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5fb6b62d684b4890\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued; exec stream closed as the node went down, confirming the reboot command was accepted\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving an actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ae6a1e947f0a4c4f\",\"cmd-a0ad3b2463064e38\"],\"summary\":\"First poll failed with connection reset (node down); subsequent poll succeeded returning new boot_id 2d40a3de..., different from the pre-reboot 92ec88af...\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required service/data (LV auto-mount, data integrity, cluster membership n/a single node)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0304711b0d34457c\",\"cmd-5484467bccd14eab\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/data auto-mounted via lvm-loopback.service (active) at 2.1G, lvs shows lvdata at <2.15g, and sha256sum -c confirmed both test files intact\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created an LVM logical volume (vgdata/lvdata) on node1, backed by two loopback-file physical volumes since no spare block device existed, formatted ext4 and mounted it at /srv/data. Wrote test data, then grew the LV online (while mounted) from ~1000MiB to ~2.15GiB via vgextend + lvextend + resize2fs, verifying data integrity throughout. Set up persistence across reboot via a systemd oneshot unit (lvm-loopback.service) that reattaches the loop devices and activates the VG before local-fs-pre.target, referenced from /etc/fstab via x-systemd.requires. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id and healthy mount/data state, issued systemctl reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified /srv/data remounted automatically at 2.1G with both test files passing sha256sum verification.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 disk layout: single 20G vda fully allocated to root/boot, no spare block device or partition available for a native PV","Created two 1200M backing files under /var/lib/lvmfiles and attached them as /dev/loop20 and /dev/loop21","pvcreate on loop20, vgcreate vgdata, lvcreate lvdata (1000M), mkfs.ext4, mounted at /srv/data","Wrote testfile.txt and bigfile.txt to /srv/data and recorded sha256 checksums","pvcreate on loop21, vgextend vgdata with loop21, lvextend +1200M, resize2fs run online while filesystem stayed mounted; final size <2.15GiB / 2.1G reported by df","Verified checksums matched post-extend and confirmed LV remained mounted read-write","Created /etc/systemd/system/lvm-loopback.service (oneshot; reattaches both loop devices, runs udevadm settle, vgchange -ay vgdata before local-fs-pre.target) and enabled it","Added /etc/fstab entry for /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata -> /srv/data with x-systemd.requires=lvm-loopback.service,nofail","Simulated boot-time reassembly by unmounting, deactivating the VG, and detaching the loop devices, then starting the service + mount -a; fixed an incorrect /sbin/udevadm path in the unit during this test; confirmed clean automatic reassembly with intact data","Captured pre-reboot boot_id (92ec88af...) and confirmed healthy mount, size, and checksums","Issued sudo systemctl reboot on node1; connection dropped confirming the command was accepted before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed new boot_id (2d40a3de...), proving an actual restart occurred","Verified post-reboot: /srv/data auto-mounted via the new systemd unit + fstab, size 2.1G (>=2GB), lvm-loopback.service active, and both test files passed sha256sum verification"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"LV mounted at /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-0a31dd120e81439e"],"summary":"df -h shows /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata mounted at /srv/data after lvcreate/mkfs/mount"},{"requirement":"LV grown to >=2GB while staying mounted","command_ids":["cmd-fad00e5e25e04d20"],"summary":"vgextend + lvextend + online resize2fs performed while /srv/data was mounted; lvextend reports growth to <2.15 GiB and df shows 2.1G on /srv/data still mounted"},{"requirement":"Contents stay intact through the extend","command_ids":["cmd-0a31dd120e81439e","cmd-ce9533c26ebe479f"],"summary":"sha256 checksums of testfile.txt and bigfile.txt recorded before extend and verified OK immediately after the online resize"},{"requirement":"Persistence mechanism configured for reboot","command_ids":["cmd-96f8c8e34768425c","cmd-d90c3127e805474d","cmd-c00e1dedd79b424c"],"summary":"systemd lvm-loopback.service enabled, fstab entry added referencing it, and a simulated teardown/reassembly (detach loops, deactivate VG, restart service, mount -a) proved the automatic reassembly logic works with data intact"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-a2babb3152494952"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 92ec88af..., confirmed /srv/data mounted at 2.1G, and sha256sum -c passed for both test files before reboot"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement / command accepted before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-5fb6b62d684b4890"],"summary":"systemctl reboot issued; exec stream closed as the node went down, confirming the reboot command was accepted"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving an actual restart","command_ids":["cmd-ae6a1e947f0a4c4f","cmd-a0ad3b2463064e38"],"summary":"First poll failed with connection reset (node down); subsequent poll succeeded returning new boot_id 2d40a3de..., different from the pre-reboot 92ec88af..."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required service/data (LV auto-mount, data integrity, cluster membership n/a single node)","command_ids":["cmd-0304711b0d34457c","cmd-5484467bccd14eab"],"summary":"After reboot, /srv/data auto-mounted via lvm-loopback.service (active) at 2.1G, lvs shows lvdata at <2.15g, and sha256sum -c confirmed both test files intact"}]},"ttft_ms":3063,"type":"result","duration_ms":199980,"uuid":"b3a3681b-841b-486d-be11-d2978b24379d","ttft_stream_ms":2309,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":3060,"queued_tur